4. GTO BASELINE PHILOSOPHY
==================================================

Do NOT invent poker strategy percentages.

Do NOT hard-code fake percentages and call them GTO.

Do NOT scrape GTO Wizard.
Do NOT copy proprietary solution datasets.

During early UI development a MOCK provider is allowed, but every mocked value must be clearly marked internally and visually as MOCK/DEMO data.

Production GTO baseline will eventually come from a mathematically generated solver pipeline.

Target long-term pipeline:

Research Game Tree
-> CFR / equilibrium solver
-> research results
-> simplified representative action tree
-> re-solve
-> versioned baseline dataset

Example baseline identifier:

CP_NL50_ANTE_100BB_BASELINE_V1

Important solver development rule:

Do not attempt to hallucinate a production-grade six-player no-limit Hold'em solver in one phase.

Create solver work as an isolated later research milestone.

First establish:
- interfaces,
- data schemas,
- test games,
- a solver-lab package or separate CLI.

For CFR correctness experiments, small games such as Kuhn/Leduc Poker may be used before attempting full Hold'em.

Before integrating any external solver:
- check license
- document license
- ensure future distribution/business model compatibility

Never silently adopt AGPL/commercial/proprietary code.

