8. STACK MODEL
==================================================

At session start:
user enters actual player stacks.

After that:
Poker Engine automatically updates stacks from actions.

Stack should always be directly editable from the table UI.

Click stack:
-> inline editor
-> number
-> Enter saves
-> Esc cancels

Auto top-up setting:

per player:
autoTopUpEnabled
topUpTargetBB

At new hand:
if enabled and stack < target:
top up to target

Do not reduce a stack that is above the target.

Example:
97 BB -> 100 BB
115 BB -> remains 115 BB

==================================================
9. DIRTY STACK / OBSERVE MODE
==================================================

When Hero is active:

mode = HERO_PLAYING

Show:
- full action input
- Hero cards
- board
- GTO panel when Hero decision is reached

If Hero folds:

automatically enter OBSERVE mode.

User may:

A. continue recording all opponent actions

If so:
stacks remain exactly tracked.

B. press SKIP REST

If SKIP REST is used:
- stop detailed state tracking for the remainder of the hand
- all players who were still capable of changing stack become DIRTY
- players who had already folded with fully known contributions remain CLEAN

On next hand:
only DIRTY stacks require resynchronization.

Do NOT show a six-field modal by default.

The stack values on the table themselves are editable.

Dirty stacks receive a subtle indicator.

When editing a dirty stack and pressing Enter:
automatically focus the next dirty stack if practical.

The user may still start a new hand with dirty stacks, but the application must visibly warn that GTO/state accuracy may be reduced.

