12. ACTION UX
==================================================

Primary actions:

F = Fold
C = Check / Call
R = Bet / Raise
A = All-in
Z = Undo
N = Next Hand

Optional:
S = toggle selected player's sit-out state, only when it cannot conflict with normal typing.

C is context-sensitive:

if call amount == 0:
CHECK

otherwise:
CALL

No separate Limp button.

A preflop call before any raise is internally classifiable as LIMP.

The user does not need to think about the classification.

R behavior:

press R
-> focus numeric input
-> user enters RAISE TO / BET TO amount in BB
-> Enter confirms
-> Esc cancels

Use "to amount" semantics.

Example:

existing street contribution = 2.5 BB
user types R 9 Enter
player's total contribution on that street becomes 9 BB

For postflop first bet:
the entered number is naturally the bet amount because prior street contribution is zero.

Show minimal useful preview:

Raise to: 9 BB
Additional: 6.5 BB
Min: X
Max: Y

Do not make user calculate pot percentages.

Engine calculates them.

